# Files in the build output that must never be uploaded as static assets.
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, so this lands at the root of the
# asset directory, where wrangler reads it. Patterns are .gitignore-style.

# Sourcemaps. vite builds with sourcemap: 'hidden' (see vite.config.ts), which
# omits the //# sourceMappingURL comment but still WRITES the .map file — and
# a map carries `sourcesContent`, i.e. the complete EMOS TypeScript source,
# verbatim, readable by anyone who appends '.map' to a bundle URL.
#
# `npm run build:deploy` already deletes these, but that only protects deploys
# that remember to use it: a plain `npm run build` in a CI build command
# silently publishes the whole source. This file is the guard that does not
# depend on anyone picking the right script — it is enforced by wrangler at
# upload time, on every deploy, however the build was invoked.
#
# Local builds keep their maps, which is the point: a captured production
# stack is still mappable by rebuilding the same SHA.
*.map
